Keep the loaded shadow colour type in range

The loader of the shadow settings checks the size and the two offsets against
their limits. It replaces a value outside those limits with the default of
the group. It gave the colour type no such check. setColorType() assigns the
number before its switch, and the default branch of that switch leaves an
unknown number in place.

A file that holds ColorType=99 therefore reached the combination box of the
window manager page. QComboBox::setCurrentIndex() refuses the index and shows
an empty box, and the next save wrote ColorType=-1 back to the file.

Replace a colour type outside the range of the box with the default of the
group. Put the new check beside the checks of the size and of the offsets. A
value from Focus to Custom loads as before.

The change sits on the branch work/wm-kcm of the local tree, as commit 3 of 4.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/kwin/qtcurveshadowconfiguration.cpp b/qt6/kwin/qtcurveshadowconfiguration.cpp
index 88fe23f4..02bd1c56 100644
--- a/qt6/kwin/qtcurveshadowconfiguration.cpp
+++ b/qt6/kwin/qtcurveshadowconfiguration.cpp
@@ -110,6 +110,8 @@ void ShadowConfig::load(KConfig *cfg)
         m_hOffset=def.horizontalOffset();
     if(m_vOffset<MIN_OFFSET || m_vOffset>MAX_OFFSET)
         m_vOffset=def.verticalOffset();
+    if(m_colorType<CT_FOCUS || m_colorType>CT_CUSTOM)
+        m_colorType=def.colorType();
     setColorType((ColorType)m_colorType);
 }
 
